WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.358 --> 00:00:05.618
Jimmy was a pauper.

2
00:00:06.198 --> 00:00:07.639
He did not have much money.

3
00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:09.800
He did not have much to eat.

4
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.001
He did not have much of anything.

5
00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:16.323
Jimmy spent many days looking for work.

6
00:00:17.143 --> 00:00:18.503
One day he met a farmer.

7
00:00:18.523 --> 00:00:20.544
"Can I work for you?"

8
00:00:21.025 --> 00:00:21.825
Jimmy asked him.

9
00:00:21.845 --> 00:00:26.087
"Yes, but you must work hard," the farmer said.

10
00:00:26.107 --> 00:00:28.928
"I promise, sir," replied Jimmy.

11
00:00:31.492 --> 00:00:32.813
Jimmy kept his promise.

12
00:00:33.593 --> 00:00:35.815
Every day Jimmy worked hard at the farm.

13
00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:38.556
The farmer and his family liked Jimmy.

14
00:00:39.257 --> 00:00:41.578
His daughter always brought him something to drink.

15
00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.681
Jimmy loved to read and study.

16
00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:50.403
He promised himself that one day, he would no longer be a pauper.

17
00:00:50.423 --> 00:00:53.925
"I am going to make my life better," he vowed.

18
00:00:53.945 --> 00:00:57.968
"One day I am going to become an important person."

19
00:01:01.164 --> 00:01:03.925
Every free moment he had, Jimmy read and studied.

20
00:01:03.945 --> 00:01:06.106
"What are you reading, Jimmy?"

21
00:01:06.847 --> 00:01:08.527
asked the farmer's daughter one day.

22
00:01:08.547 --> 00:01:12.249
"It's a book about Napoleon," answered Jimmy.

23
00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:17.551
Every day the farmer's daughter came to talk with Jimmy.

24
00:01:18.132 --> 00:01:21.673
They talked about books, nature, travel, and their dreams.

25
00:01:22.574 --> 00:01:24.134
They began to like each other.

26
00:01:25.055 --> 00:01:27.416
The farmer did not know what was going on.

27
00:01:29.344 --> 00:01:31.946
When he saw them together, everything changed.

28
00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:34.187
"What is going on!"

29
00:01:34.748 --> 00:01:35.728
the farmer shouted.

30
00:01:35.748 --> 00:01:41.512
"Please, sir, I Jimmy tried to explain, but the farmer refused to listen.

31
00:01:46.616 --> 00:01:48.377
daughter will not marry a pauper!"

32
00:01:48.937 --> 00:01:49.898
the farmer shouted.

33
00:01:50.739 --> 00:01:52.740
Then the farmer ordered Jimmy to leave.

34
00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.401
"Get out!

35
00:01:54.741 --> 00:01:55.582
How dare you!

36
00:01:56.242 --> 00:01:58.184
You are not welcome here anymore!"

37
00:01:58.720 --> 00:01:59.341
he shouted.

38
00:02:00.061 --> 00:02:02.863
Poor Jimmy could not say another word to the farmer.

39
00:02:03.844 --> 00:02:06.245
He turned around and left without looking back.

40
00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:12.990
One day, 35 years later, the farmer was cleaning out the stable.

41
00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.772
He found an old bag and some books.

42
00:02:18.573 --> 00:02:20.415
The books used to belong to Jimmy.

43
00:02:21.055 --> 00:02:22.856
The farmer opened one of the books.

44
00:02:23.557 --> 00:02:24.998
He was very surprised.

45
00:02:25.878 --> 00:02:28.100
There was a name written inside the book.

46
00:02:28.792 --> 00:02:31.354
It read: James Abram Garfield.

47
00:02:35.357 --> 00:02:38.540
James Abram Garfield was the name of the president.

48
00:02:39.221 --> 00:02:41.122
Jimmy was a nickname for James.

49
00:02:41.923 --> 00:02:43.484
The farmer could not believe it!

50
00:02:44.545 --> 00:02:48.108
Jimmy the pauper was James Garfield─the president!

51
00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:55.774
That day the farmer learned an important lesson: Never judge a book by its cover.

52
00:02:56.654 --> 00:03:00.050
You should not judge people by the way they look.

53
00:03:01.572 --> 00:03:03.495
Jimmy kept his promise to himself.

54
00:03:04.175 --> 00:03:06.999
After leaving the farm, he studied and worked hard.

55
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:10.123
He did indeed become an important person.

56
00:03:11.105 --> 00:03:16.051
He went from a life as a pauper to become the twentieth president of the United States.
